        {
          "path": "_m/9/y/g/x/wamego-wk/wamego-banner.jpg",
          "filename": "Wamego banner.jpg",
          "caption": "Journeyman Linemen from Bluestem Electric Cooperative build a new electric service for a new home outside of Olsburg, Kansas. \nThis Rural Development investment is part of an investment to build 30 miles of line, improve 44 miles and make other system improvements. The loan amount includes $144,000 for smart grid projects. \nBluestem Electric is headquartered in Wamego, which serves 5,542 residential consumers, 1,364 commercial consumers and 201 irrigation systems. \nBluestem operates and maintains 3,000 miles of line in 11 counties.\n\nUSDA Photo by Preston Keres",
